# Walkthrough: Expanded Delegation Access

We have successfully expanded the access permissions for the Delegation Management page. Previously, while the sidebar link was visible to some roles, the backend data was restricted exclusively to the Administrator role.

## Changes Made

### 1. Backend Route Authorization
- Updated `server/src/routes/delegation.routes.ts` to allow multiple roles to access delegation endpoints.
- **Allowed Roles**: `ADMINISTRATOR`, `OPERATIONS_MANAGER`, `GENERAL_MANAGER`, `CTO`, and `HOD_PROJECTS`.

### 2. Frontend Route Protection
- Updated `src/App.tsx` to include `ADMINISTRATOR` in the `allowedRoles` list for the `/delegation` route.
- This ensures that Admins can also access the page (they were previously missing from the frontend allowed list).

### 3. Sidebar Visibility
- Updated `src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx` to include `ADMINISTRATOR` in the `allowedRoles` for the Delegation navigation item.

## Verification

### Role Access
- **Operations Manager (OM)**: Can now view the delegation status of all approvers and update their absence/substitute status.
- **Administrator**: Retains full access to the delegation management tools.
- **Other Approvers**: GM, CTO, and HOD Projects now have the same management capabilities as the OM and Admin.

> [!TIP]
> Users may need to refresh their browser or log out and back in to pick up the new role-based permissions in their session.
